issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible : 4.5.1, 4.6.1\nNot reproducible : 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Pop!_OS 22.04 jammy (x86-64), Godot v4.6.1.stable.flathub [14d19694e]\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen checking if a process is running, it raises an error even if the process exists. But, it seems like raising an error only when it believes the process is not running.\n\n```\n    var is_running = OS.is_process_running(%SpinBox.value)\n    print([\"Is processing running: \", is_running])\n\n    is_running = OS.is_process_running(OS.get_process_id())\n    print([\"Is processing running: \", is_running])\n```\n\nMaybe I'm wrong, but I expect the `is_process_running` to just return false or true, not to raise an error if the id I passed is not running ; no matter the reason it's not running, not existing for example.\n\nI believe the issue to be from this commit (not sure though) : https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/d5738b5cdd43cb5e5f118cc206af6b2a711169f2\n\nIt changed the code where the issue is links to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f62fdbde15035c5576dad93e586201f4d41ef0cb/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp#L853\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start the 4.5.1 project and enter a PID (a real one or fake one, it doesn't seem to change anything)\n2. See the error in the logs\n3. Start the 4.4.1 project\n4. See the lack of errors.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nYou will find two projects, one with 4.4.1 and one with 4.5.1. One working as expected, one raising errors.\n[test_process.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25894757/test_process.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gra